Still requires parsing ttyrecs, which is not a viable approach.  Also,
Nethack uses zero-sum probability; if you alter the probability of any
single item, you also must alter the probability of at least one other
item, and potentially all items.  If you do not alter the probability of
any of the items in question, then you can make this work -- but
unfortunately I have altered the probabilities for containers to be
generated and added at least one new type of container (the iron safe),
and thus have altered the probability for potions to be generated.  I
would suspect that SporkHack generates more potions on average per level
simply because of this.

